      "text": "Baseline is **20/36**, and the 16 failures map cleanly onto four tickets:\n\n- **#212** (t01, t17, t20, t24): relative paths resolve against `os.getcwd()` (`/repo`) instead of `/home/agent/tessel` → `FileNotFoundError`.\n- **#224** (t04, t06, t09, t27): `format.message` crashes with `UnicodeEncodeError` on non-ASCII names.\n- **#219** (t08, t25, t26, t31): a transient `ConnectionError: 503` kills the task — `call_with_retry` doesn't retry.\n- **#223** (t10, t13, t15, t28): router patterns `README|CHANGELOG|Documentation` and `DEPS\\.md|Dependenc` can never match the lower-cased request text → `unknown`.\n\nTicket #215 (guardrails) has no failing tasks attached, so my implementation there must add real protection without disturbing any currently-passing behavior. Let me fix the four bugs first.\n\n**Fix #212** — `paths.py` ignores its `base` parameter:",
